![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

If any required `source_page_render_id` is missing from `renderResultsById`, it is silently filtered out. This can cause `renderedCount === renderResults.length` to evaluate to `true` even when a required page was not rendered, leading to a false-positive success status. Explicitly track and record missing render results as blockers.

```javascript
    const requiredIds = asArray(row.source_page_render_ids);
    const renderResults = requiredIds.map((id) => renderResultsById.get(id)).filter(Boolean);
    const missingIds = requiredIds.filter((id) => !renderResultsById.has(id));
    const renderBlockers = renderResults
      .filter((result) => result.render_status !== 'rendered')
      .map((result) => ({ 
        blocker_id: result.failure_class,
        failure_class: result.failure_class,
        source_page_render_id: result.source_page_render_id,
        source_pdf_path: result.source_pdf_path,
        page_number_1based: result.page_number_1based,
        reason: result.failure_reason ?? null,
      }));
    const missingBlockers = missingIds.map((id) => ({ 
      blocker_id: 'missing_render_result',
      failure_class: 'missing_render_result',
      source_page_render_id: id,
    }));
    const blockers = [...existingBlockers, ...renderBlockers, ...missingBlockers];
```

