![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Calling `getImageData(x, y, 1, 1)` inside a nested loop is a major performance bottleneck because of the high overhead of individual canvas context calls. Instead, retrieve the entire image data buffer once with `getImageData(0, 0, width, height)` and index into it directly.

```javascript
function estimateNonblankPixelSignal(renderCanvas) {
  const context = renderCanvas.getContext('2d');
  const width = renderCanvas.width;
  const height = renderCanvas.height;
  if (width === 0 || height === 0) return 0;
  const imgData = context.getImageData(0, 0, width, height).data;
  const sampleStepX = Math.max(1, Math.floor(width / 20));
  const sampleStepY = Math.max(1, Math.floor(height / 20));
  let nonblank = 0;
  for (let y = 0; y < height; y += sampleStepY) {
    for (let x = 0; x < width; x += sampleStepX) {
      const idx = (y * width + x) * 4;
      const red = imgData[idx];
      const green = imgData[idx + 1];
      const blue = imgData[idx + 2];
      const alpha = imgData[idx + 3];
      if (alpha > 0 && (red < 250 || green < 250 || blue < 250)) nonblank += 1;
    }
  }
  return nonblank;
}
```

